-- title:
--   Transversal integral of the unramified twisted unipotent term as a pure tensor
-- statement:
--   Setting. Let $K$ and $L$ be number fields with $L$ Galois over $K$, let $\nu_{Z_L}$ be a Haar measure on the idele group $(\mathbb{A}_L)^\times$, let $D$ be an idele Galois descent datum for $L/K$ (a homomorphism $\mathrm{Gal}(L/K) \to \mathrm{Aut}_{\mathrm{ring}}(\mathbb{A}_L)$ whose members are continuous and compatible with the action on $L$ through $L \to \mathbb{A}_L$), and let $\sigma \in \mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ satisfy `hgen`: every element of $\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ lies in the subgroup generated by the powers of $\sigma$. Let $S_L$ be a finite set of finite places of $L$ satisfying `hSL`: every $w$ with $e(w \mid w \cap \mathcal{O}_K) \neq 1$ lies in $S_L$. Let $\xi_L$ be a homomorphism from the full unit group of $\mathbb{A}_L$ (realised as the top subgroup) to $\mathbb{C}^\times$, subject to `hξc` (continuity of $z \mapsto \xi_L(z)$ as a complex-valued function), `hξt` (triviality on the image of $L^\times$) and `hξσ` (invariance under the automorphism of $(\mathbb{A}_L)^\times$ induced by $D$ at $\sigma$). Let $S$ be a finite set of finite places of $K$, $\varphi_a$ a function on $\mathrm{GL}_2$ of the infinite adeles of $L$, and $\varphi_S$ a family of functions on $\mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K K_v)$ indexed by the finite places $v$ of $K$; let $\mu_K$ be an additive Haar measure on $\mathbb{A}_K$.
--
--   Hecke data. Let $T$ be a finite set of finite places of $K$ satisfying `hT`: no place of $L$ above a place of $T$ belongs to $S_L$. For each finite place $v$ of $K$ let $w_v$ be a chosen place of $L$ above $v$ (`ws`), let $n_v \in \mathbb{N}$ (`ns`), let $r_{T,v} : \mathrm{Fin}(n_v) \to \mathrm{GL}_2(L_{w_v})$ (`rTs`) and let $z_v \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L_{w_v})$ (`zs`). Let $S_\tau$ be a finite set of finite places of $K$ characterised by `hSτ`: $v \in S_\tau$ if and only if either $v \in S$ and $v \notin T$, or some place of $L$ above $v$ is ramified over $v$.
--
--   Transversal data. Let $n \in \mathbb{N}$, let $c : \mathrm{Fin}(n) \to \mathbb{R}$, let $\tau_j$ be Borel measures on $(\mathbb{A}_L)^\times$, let $\tau^{\mathrm{fin}}_{j,v}$ be measures on $(L \otimes_K K_v)^\times$, let $\tau^{\mathrm{arch}}_{j,v}$ be measures on the unit group of $\prod_{w \mid v} L_w$ for $v$ an infinite place of $K$, and let $\pi_{j,v} \in (L \otimes_K K_v)^\times$. The hypotheses on these are: `hcpos`, $c_j > 0$; `hlev`, $\tau_j$ is carried by the locus where the idele norm equals $c_j$; `hτfin`, each $\tau_j$ is finite on compact sets; `hτ0`, $\tau_j$ vanishes off the set of $t$ such that for every $v \notin S_\tau$ the semi-local component of $t$ at $v$ lies in the product of the integral units (the units of the image of $\mathcal{O}_L \otimes_{\mathcal{O}_K} \mathcal{O}_{K_v}$) with the image of the local units of $K_v$; `hgood`, for $v \notin S_\tau$ the measure $\tau^{\mathrm{fin}}_{j,v}$ is a Haar measure restricted to the integral units and normalised by their volume; `hgood'`, for $v \notin S_\tau$ the measure $\tau^{\mathrm{fin}}_{j,v}$ gives mass $0$ to the complement of the integral units and mass $1$ to them; `hbad`, for $v \in S_\tau$ the measure $\tau^{\mathrm{fin}}_{j,v}$ is the translate by $\pi_{j,v}$ of the pushforward to $(L \otimes_K K_v)^\times$ of a Haar measure on the subgroup of elements whose $K_v$-norm has valuation zero; `harch`, each $\tau^{\mathrm{arch}}_{j,v}$ is the pushforward of a Haar measure on the subgroup of elements of norm one; and `hfac3`, a factorisation identity asserting that for every finite set $S_f \supseteq S_\tau$ and all measurable families $f_v$ on $(L \otimes_K K_v)^\times$ ($v \in S_f$) and $g_v$ on the archimedean semi-local unit groups, the lower integral against $\tau_j$ of $\bigl(\prod_v g_v(\text{archimedean semi-local component})\bigr)\bigl(\prod_{v \in S_f} f_v(\text{semi-local component})\bigr)$ times the indicator of the set of $t$ whose semi-local components are integral at all $v \notin S_f$ equals $\bigl(\prod_v \int g_v \, d\tau^{\mathrm{arch}}_{j,v}\bigr)\prod_{v \in S_f} \int f_v \, d\tau^{\mathrm{fin}}_{j,v}$.
--
--   Conclusion. There exist a finite set $S_x$ of finite places of $K$, functions $g_j$ on the infinite adeles of $K$, and functions $h_{0,j,v}$ on $K_v$, such that the following three assertions hold.
--
--   First, $S \cup T \subseteq S_x$.
--
--   Secondly, for all $k_\bullet, j_\bullet : \{\text{finite places of } K\} \to \mathbb{N}$ and every index $j$, the function
--   $$\Psi_{j}(x) \;=\; \mathbf{1}_{\{x \,:\, x_v \in \mathcal{O}_{K_v} \text{ for all } v \notin S_x\}}(x)\; g_j(x_\infty) \prod_{v \in S_x} F_{j,v}(x_v),$$
--   where $F_{j,v} =$ [`twistedLocalFactor`](def/TwistedUnipotentTerm_SemiLocalOrbitalVocab.html#L85) $K\,L\,D\,\sigma\,\xi_L\,v\,w_v\,n_v\,r_{T,v}\,z_v\,k_v\,j_v$ if $v \in T$ and $F_{j,v} = h_{0,j,v}$ otherwise, lies in the Schwartz–Bruhat space of $K$ (the $\mathbb{C}$-span of pure tensors of a Schwartz function on the mixed space with a locally constant compactly supported function on the finite adeles) and has compact support. Here [`twistedLocalFactor`](def/TwistedUnipotentTerm_SemiLocalOrbitalVocab.html#L85) is the local trace pushforward from $L \otimes_K K_v$ to $K_v$ of the semi-local unipotent orbital function of the word, namely of the function obtained by integrating the semi-local character attached to $\xi_L$ against the integral over the semi-local integral set of the word indicator associated with the data $(w_v, n_v, r_{T,v}, z_v, k_v, j_v)$.
--
--   Thirdly, for all $k_\bullet, j_\bullet$, every $\varphi$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ and every $\varphi_f$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2$ of the finite adeles of $L$ such that `IsSemiLocalFactorization` $K\,L\,(S \cup T)$ holds for $\varphi$, $\varphi_a$, $\varphi_f$ and the local data which at $v \in T$ is
--   $$x \;\mapsto\; \sum_{\iota : \mathrm{Fin}(k_v) \to \mathrm{Fin}(n_v)} \mathbf{1}_{\text{semi-local integral set}}\Bigl(\bigl(\text{semi-local component at } v \text{ of the local embedding of } \textstyle\prod_{m} r_{T,v}(\iota(m)) \cdot z_v^{\,j_v}\bigr)^{-1} x\Bigr)$$
--   and is $\varphi_S(v)$ for $v \notin T$ (this factorisation asserts that $\varphi_a$ is an archimedean test factor, $\varphi_f$ is locally constant with compact support, the data at places of $S \cup T$ are locally constant with compact support, $\varphi_f(h)$ equals the product of the local data over $S \cup T$ when all components outside $S \cup T$ are integral and vanishes otherwise, and $\varphi$ is the product of $\varphi_a$ and $\varphi_f$ on the archimedean and finite parts), the following two statements hold for every index $j$ and every $r \in \mathbb{A}_K$. Writing
--   $$G_{t,k,\zeta}(u) \;=\; \varphi\bigl(k^{-1} \, n(u\,t^{-1}) \, \mathrm{diag}(\sigma_D(t)t^{-1}, 1) \, z(\sigma_D(\zeta)) \, \sigma_D(k)\bigr), \qquad u \in \mathbb{A}_L,$$
--   where $n(\cdot)$ is the upper unipotent matrix, $\mathrm{diag}(a,1)$ the diagonal embedding, $z(\cdot)$ the central scalar embedding, $\sigma_D$ the action of $D$ at $\sigma$ on ideles and on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ entrywise, and $k$ runs over the maximal compact subgroup of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ (finite part integral, archimedean parts row isometries) with its Haar measure `maximalCompactHaar`:
--
--   (a) the iterated lower integral
--   $$\int^{-}\!\!\int^{-}\!\!\int^{-} \bigl\| \xi_L(\zeta)\, (\text{tracePushforward}\, G_{t,k,\zeta})(r) \bigr\|_e \, d\nu_{Z_L}(\zeta)\, dk\, d\tau_j(t)$$
--   is not $\top$, where the trace pushforward of a function $F$ on $\mathbb{A}_L$ is $r \mapsto \int F(\mathrm{traceFibre}(r, w'))$ over $w'$ in the product of $\dim_K \ker(\mathrm{Tr}_{L/K})$ copies of $\mathbb{A}_K$ with the product adelic additive Haar measure; and
--
--   (b) the corresponding iterated Bochner integral
--   $$\int \Bigl( \int \Bigl( \int \xi_L(\zeta)\, (\text{tracePushforward}\, G_{t,k,\zeta})(r) \, d\nu_{Z_L}(\zeta) \Bigr) dk \Bigr) d\tau_j(t)$$
--   equals $\Psi_j(r)$, the value at $r$ of the indicator-times-product expression of the second assertion.
--
--   This is the transversal-integral step for the unipotent-type contribution in the twisted trace formula for a cyclic extension $L/K$ at Hecke places that are unramified and outside the bad set: it identifies the triple integral of the twisted unipotent term, pushed forward along the trace, as a single compactly supported Schwartz–Bruhat function on $\mathbb{A}_K$ which is a pure tensor whose factors at the Hecke places are the twisted local factors of the corresponding word, uniformly in the word profile $(k_v, j_v)$. It is used in the assembly of the finite-sum difference identity [`AutomorphicForm.TwistedBruhat.exists_forall_integral_transversal_finsum_tracePushforward_sub_eq_finsum_indicator_prod_twistedLocalFactor_sub_unram`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.TwistedBruhat.exists_forall_integral_transversal_finsum_tracePushforward_sub_eq_finsum_indicator_prod_twistedLocalFactor_sub_unram).
